@ImpossibleTravel38   Thank you.  This is from an article in today's SF Chronicle:

"In May, San Francisco Mayor Daniel Lurie touted an official estimate showing a sharp drop in the number of people living on the street. But new details about the tally reveal a more complicated picture of the city’s push to combat homelessness.
Almost half of those surveyed along with the count said they were homeless when they arrived in San Francisco, a record high. Critics of the city’s drug policies have long argued that homeless people in San Francisco — about a third of whom report dealing with addiction — often come for what one of Lurie’s department heads has described as “drug tourism.”"
